# No tracked Cargo.lock here (fleet rule). A lock may only ever freeze EXTERNAL
# dependencies; this crate's lock froze an INTERNAL fork —
# `AdaWorldAPI/ndarray branch=master#c6262d63ec01d92490343b5698c3cd2727dfea7e`
# — while `Cargo.toml` correctly asked for the floating branch. Measured
# 2026-10-10: that commit is not even an ancestor of ndarray's master (it was
# squashed/rebased away), and master had moved on by six weeks.
#
# This ignore lives in the crate directory, not the repository root: the root
# `.gitignore` is upstream's file, and editing it would add a conflict surface
# to every future upstream sync for no benefit.
#
# The repository root's own `Cargo.lock` and `fuzz/Cargo.lock` are deliberately
# NOT covered. They are upstream's, they are how a published binary pins its
# build, and they were measured to contain zero `git+` sources — they lock only
# external crates.io dependencies, which the rule permits.
Cargo.lock
